      'Gifting the family home and continuing to live there without paying fair-market rent.',
      'Gifting low-basis assets the donor would otherwise have held until death; the heirs may pay more capital gains tax than the estate tax saved.',
      'Deathbed transfers of life insurance or releases of retained powers.',
      'Gifts the donor cannot afford, leading to implied agreements to return funds, which courts treat as retained enjoyment.',
      'Gifts to a spouse who is not a US citizen (limited marital deduction) or gifts to trusts without proper Crummey powers for annual exclusion treatment.',
