      'A family constitution (charter, protocol) is a statement of values, decision-making processes and expectations. On its own it is a moral and relational document, not a contract. It becomes enforceable only to the extent its provisions are written into instruments that do bind: the operating or shareholder agreement of the family company, the trust instrument, employment agreements and the charters of family entities. Good governance design uses the constitution to set policy and the legal documents to execute it.',
