    taxConsequence: 'Powers held by beneficiaries over their own interests risk §2041 inclusion; powers held by the grantor risk §2036/§2038; independent-party powers are generally safe. Grantor-trust status can be affected by who holds which powers (§674).',
    assetProtectionConsequence: 'Beneficiaries who hold distribution powers over themselves weaken spendthrift protection; independent trustees or advisers holding discretion preserve it.',
    documentation: ['Trust instrument with directed trust and protector provisions', 'Family council charter aligned with the instrument', 'Adviser acceptance and fiduciary acknowledgments', 'Direction letters and trustee acknowledgments', 'Minutes of council decisions'],
